WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.646 --> 00:00:13.288
Mother enjoyed a quiet time with her two younger daughters that evening.

2
00:00:14.369 --> 00:00:19.533
She mended some old clothes to take to the Hummels, while Beth patched up her dolls to give

3
00:00:19.593 --> 00:00:21.254
to the little girls in that family.

4
00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.516
Amy was unusually calm and silent.

5
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:27.658
She kept her nose in her book the whole time.

6
00:00:27.678 --> 00:00:29.940
"Are you feeling all right, dear?"

7
00:00:30.344 --> 00:00:31.425
Mother asked worriedly.

8
00:00:31.445 --> 00:00:33.505
"I'm fine, Mother.

9
00:00:33.946 --> 00:00:37.207
Just a little tired is all," was Amy's reply.

10
00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:41.929
Beth glanced at her sister with concern but did not say anything.

11
00:00:43.149 --> 00:00:47.091
At around 10:30, Meg and Jo returned from their evening out with Laurie.

12
00:00:47.111 --> 00:00:50.952
"We're back!"

13
00:00:51.373 --> 00:00:56.655
Jo announced loudly, in case anybody didn't hear them happily chatting away outside the door.

14
00:00:56.675 --> 00:01:01.217
"Come and tell us how your evening was," Mother called out warmly.

15
00:01:01.957 --> 00:01:07.820
Meg and Jo entered the living room, their cheeks flushed with delight and their eyes sparkling like diamonds.

16
00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:15.803
"Oh, Mother, it was absolutely beautiful," Meg praised, clasping her delicate hands against her chest.

17
00:01:15.823 --> 00:01:24.207
"Well, I thought the costumes were a bit exaggerated," commented Jo critically, but then she started to laugh

18
00:01:24.287 --> 00:01:25.768
as she recalled a funny moment.

19
00:01:27.096 --> 00:01:32.358
"In one scene, the lights wouldn't come on so the characters didn't know who was standing where.

20
00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:37.839
Then finally, when the lights did turn on, well, they were all in the wrong place.

21
00:01:38.759 --> 00:01:41.760
So everyone kind of ran around trying to find their positions.

22
00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.001
We nearly fell out of our seats laughing."

23
00:01:46.101 --> 00:01:49.202
Everyone except Amy thought Jo's description was funny.

24
00:01:49.222 --> 00:01:51.843
"Are you still mad at me, Amy?"

25
00:01:52.223 --> 00:01:55.564
Jo sat next to her sister and teasingly reached to touch her hair.

26
00:01:56.468 --> 00:02:02.672
Moving her head out of Jo's reach, Amy replied coolly, "As you can see, we, too, have enjoyed

27
00:02:02.712 --> 00:02:04.153
a lovely evening at home.

28
00:02:05.414 --> 00:02:08.516
It was nice to be alone with Mother and Beth for a change."

29
00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:10.258
"That's good.

30
00:02:10.638 --> 00:02:11.819
No hard feelings, then?"

31
00:02:12.199 --> 00:02:13.940
Jo held out her hand like a man.

32
00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:20.305
Looking at her sister with disdain, Amy ignored her hand but said, "No hard feelings."

33
00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:24.828
Mother watched the exchange between her two daughters uneasily.

34
00:02:25.852 --> 00:02:30.615
She could feel something was not right and wondered whether a major fight was brewing.

35
00:02:32.196 --> 00:02:34.037
Yawning, Jo stood up and stretched.

36
00:02:34.057 --> 00:02:36.438
"I'm going to bed.

37
00:02:36.818 --> 00:02:37.559
Good night, all."

38
00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:42.241
"I think I'll turn in as well," said Meg.

39
00:02:43.602 --> 00:02:48.765
As they walked up together to their room, Meg turned to Jo and said, "Did you think Amy

40
00:02:48.805 --> 00:02:50.066
was acting strangely?"

41
00:02:50.806 --> 00:02:54.168
Jo shrugged and replied, "It's obvious she's still mad at me.

42
00:02:54.624 --> 00:02:55.745
But she'll get over it."

43
00:02:56.805 --> 00:03:01.207
With such an exciting evening, the girls had forgotten about Amy's threat.

44
00:03:02.027 --> 00:03:05.849
The next day, however, they would remember it all too well.

45
00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:12.692
On Saturday mornings, Mother allowed the girls to sleep in while she and Hannah prepared their favorite breakfast.

46
00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:15.974
That day Meg was the first one to come down.

47
00:03:15.994 --> 00:03:17.654
"Good morning.

48
00:03:17.854 --> 00:03:18.775
Did you sleep well?"

49
00:03:19.055 --> 00:03:20.856
Mother greeted her eldest with a kiss.

50
00:03:22.084 --> 00:03:23.344
"Wonderfully, thank you.

51
00:03:23.805 --> 00:03:27.406
Last night was so magical," Meg replied dreamily.

52
00:03:27.426 --> 00:03:29.266
"Is Jo still in bed?"

53
00:03:29.606 --> 00:03:30.107
asked Mother.

54
00:03:30.927 --> 00:03:34.908
Shaking her head Meg answered, "She's up but she must be in the attic."

55
00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:41.930
No sooner had Meg spoken these words when Jo burst into the room, in her writer's outfit─ old

56
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:47.112
red knitted hat, smelly oversized gray cardigan, and her gloves with the fingers cut out.

57
00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:52.882
Everyone would have laughed at her comical entrance but for the panic written all over her face.

58
00:03:52.902 --> 00:03:55.163
"Jo, what is the matter?"

59
00:03:55.503 --> 00:03:56.604
Mother asked, alarmed.

60
00:03:56.624 --> 00:03:59.165
"I can't find it.

61
00:03:59.765 --> 00:04:02.746
It's gone," Jo said in a trembling voice.

62
00:04:03.887 --> 00:04:05.007
"What's gone, darling?"

63
00:04:05.348 --> 00:04:07.689
Mother tried to calm her shaking daughter.

64
00:04:07.709 --> 00:04:09.869
"My story.

65
00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.271
The one I've been working on for the past two years.

66
00:04:13.651 --> 00:04:18.245
The one I was writing for Father," Jo replied, not sounding like Jo at all.

67
00:04:18.265 --> 00:04:21.286
"What do you mean it's gone?

68
00:04:21.726 --> 00:04:23.486
Are you sure you didn't misplace it?"

69
00:04:23.766 --> 00:04:24.387
Mother asked.

70
00:04:24.407 --> 00:04:27.127
"I keep it in my drawer upstairs.

71
00:04:27.668 --> 00:04:28.688
Everyone knows that.

72
00:04:29.408 --> 00:04:35.030
Why would Jo suddenly stopped abruptly, her face white and pained.

73
00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:43.164
"Jo, Jo, please calm down," said Meg, who was thinking the exact same thing as Jo, but wanted

74
00:04:43.284 --> 00:04:46.445
desperately to prevent her sister from doing something drastic.

75
00:04:46.465 --> 00:04:50.566
"That little witch," Jo muttered under her breath.

76
00:04:51.327 --> 00:04:55.868
She pulled her hat off and threw it hard as she sprinted out of the kitchen screaming madly.

77
00:04:56.968 --> 00:05:02.650
At that unfortunate moment, Beth and Amy, awakened by the commotion, came down to see what was causing

78
00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:03.270
all the noise.

79
00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.051
"What did you do with it?"

80
00:05:06.391 --> 00:05:08.252
Jo yelled as soon as she saw Amy.

81
00:05:09.328 --> 00:05:10.949
"Jo! What is the matter with you?"

82
00:05:11.269 --> 00:05:13.190
Mother grabbed her wild daughter's arm.

83
00:05:14.271 --> 00:05:19.654
Instead of denying she had anything to do with what was making her sister so angry, Amy pressed

84
00:05:19.694 --> 00:05:21.616
her lips together and remained silent.

85
00:05:22.556 --> 00:05:24.797
"Amy?" Mother looked at her, puzzled.

86
00:05:25.498 --> 00:05:27.759
"Do you know what happened to Jo's story?

87
00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.161
If you do, you must speak now."

88
00:05:31.181 --> 00:05:35.284
Wearing a nasty expression, Amy uttered, "I burned it."

89
00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:41.541
The silence that followed was louder than if they had all been screaming at the top of their

90
00:05:41.581 --> 00:05:44.342
lungs. "What?"

91
00:05:44.922 --> 00:05:46.723
Jo's voice cracked in agony.

92
00:05:46.743 --> 00:05:49.323
"I burned your stupid story.

93
00:05:49.684 --> 00:05:52.324
I told you I would get you back," Amy spat.

94
00:05:53.344 --> 00:05:58.886
Pulling away from her mother's grasp, Jo stomped over to Amy, and slapped her hard across the face.

95
00:05:59.866 --> 00:06:05.708
Then without another word, she ran blindly out of the kitchen, her cries of sorrow spreading throughout the

96
00:06:05.748 --> 00:06:09.193
house. "Jo!

97
00:06:09.633 --> 00:06:12.556
Jo!" Mother ran after her distressed daughter.

98
00:06:13.917 --> 00:06:17.520
Holding her red cheek, Amy burst into tears as well.

99
00:06:18.361 --> 00:06:23.405
Wanting to shake her and comfort her at the same time, Meg pulled Amy close to her and

100
00:06:23.465 --> 00:06:25.707
said, "You have done a wicked thing, Amy.

101
00:06:26.408 --> 00:06:28.349
I don't know if Jo will ever forgive you."

102
00:06:30.191 --> 00:06:35.556
That day, Jo locked herself in the attic, refusing to eat or even speak to anyone.

103
00:06:36.612 --> 00:06:41.273
No one had ever seen her so disheartened, and it worried everyone tremendously.

104
00:06:42.454 --> 00:06:48.135
After Amy realized how grave her actions were, she quickly began to worry about how she could get

105
00:06:48.195 --> 00:06:49.115
Jo to forgive her.

106
00:06:49.136 --> 00:06:52.476
"Do you think Jo will come down for dinner?"

107
00:06:52.837 --> 00:06:53.937
she asked childishly.

108
00:06:53.957 --> 00:06:59.758
"She has just lost the most precious thing in her life," Mother spoke to her sternly.

109
00:06:59.778 --> 00:07:03.139
"Do you think she would be thinking about food at this time?"

110
00:07:03.159 --> 00:07:05.300
"I'm sorry.

111
00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:06.960
I wasn't thinking.

112
00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:11.242
I was just so angry at the time," Amy tried to explain.

113
00:07:11.262 --> 00:07:16.823
"It's not me you should be apologizing to," was Mother's cool reply.

114
00:07:16.843 --> 00:07:19.624
"Should I go up and see her?"

115
00:07:20.004 --> 00:07:20.624
Amy sniffed.

116
00:07:21.504 --> 00:07:22.625
"Let her be, Amy.

117
00:07:23.005 --> 00:07:25.445
Just let her be," Beth said sadly.

118
00:07:26.306 --> 00:07:28.606
"Do you think Jo will ever speak to me again?"

119
00:07:29.106 --> 00:07:34.368
Amy continued with her questions, hoping that someone would say something to ease her troubled heart.

120
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:40.907
However, no one could provide the words Amy wanted to hear, for what she had done was so

121
00:07:40.987 --> 00:07:44.350
horrible that no one blamed Jo for the way she was feeling.

122
00:07:45.612 --> 00:07:47.234
Amy regretted it miserably.

123
00:07:47.254 --> 00:07:48.856
"What have I done?"
